      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This is twice the maximum, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max IR dose.\n- **1,700 mg per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** Please tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional."
      }
